Accept an emulated CAL partition (block2mtd) besides OneNAND.

libcal only accepted MTD_NANDFLASH, the N900's OneNAND. Phones without NAND,
such as the F(x)tec Pro1X, attach a small file through block2mtd as
/dev/mtd1, which reports MTD_RAM. Everything else libcal does works on it:
MEMGETBADBLOCK returns 0 (no bad blocks), MEMERASE fills with 0xFF, and a
failing OTPSELECT is already tolerated. NAND devices behave as before.

Also return an error when the type is rejected: rv still held 0 from the
successful MEMGETINFO, so callers took the failed init for a success.

--- a/src/cal.c
+++ b/src/cal.c
@@ -446,9 +446,11 @@ cal_nand_init(struct cal *c)
     goto err;
   }

-  if ( c->mtd_info.type != MTD_NANDFLASH )
+  /* MTD_RAM: CAL emulated with block2mtd on devices without NAND. */
+  if ( c->mtd_info.type != MTD_NANDFLASH && c->mtd_info.type != MTD_RAM )
   {
-    cal_error("Only NAND devices supported");
+    cal_error("Only NAND devices (or block2mtd) supported");
+    rv = -1;
     goto err;
   }

